// AssistWithBody Let the Director read or act on your Worlds, step by step (server-sent events)
//
// Runs claude-opus-5 over the operations marked `x-assist`, calling each through this
// API's MCP tools with **your** key: scopes, grants, rate limits, the write quota and
// refusals apply as if you had called it. `look` offers only `x-assist: read` tools and
// works with a read key; `act` needs `write`. Keys, webhooks, grants, billing, sign-up
// and watching are never offered. Calls outside `worlds`/`hands`, or a createWorld
// without `allowCreate`, are denied before they are made. Each step streams as it
// happens; the stream ends with `stop`. Your prompt and the answers of its calls are
// sent to Anthropic; your schedule-bit key is not.
//
// **Whose Anthropic key.** Send your own in `anthropicKey` and the run is on your
// Anthropic account: the key is used for this request only, never stored, logged or
// streamed back, and the run is not counted against your plan's assists or the
// deployment's daily ceiling (it still takes the one-run lease and every per-run bound).
// Without one, the run spends the deployment's ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and is counted. `open`
// says which (`key`). If Anthropic refuses your key, the stream ends with a `problem`
// titled `Assistant Key Rejected`, then `stop`, and the run counts as one of the
// workspace's key checks (see `assistKeyCheck`); with those spent, a run on your own key
// answers 429 until they refill. 503 when there is no key to run on (none sent, none
// configured), while the assistant is switched off, or, for a run on the deployment's
// key, once its daily ceiling is spent.
//
// One assist runs at a time per key. There is no resume: a dropped stream stops the
// run, and the calls already made stand (the journal shows them). A keepalive comment
