// AssistKeyCheckWithBody Check an Anthropic key before a run spends it
//
// Asks Anthropic whether it takes the key, the cheapest way there is: one page of its
// Models API, which spends no tokens. The key is used for that question only, never
// stored or logged, and the answer does not repeat it. Anthropic out of reach answers
// 200 with `valid: false` and a `detail` that says the key was not checked, so a client
// reads one shape; try again. Rate-limited and metered like any read; needs `read`.
// Each check is also a call to Anthropic from this deployment, so a workspace has
// Anthropic keys judged at most 10 times a minute and 100 times a UTC day (checks, and
// runs on your own key that Anthropic refused); past that, 429 with `Retry-After`.
// 503 while the assistant is switched off.
